hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"258","Wa qāla ṣallā Allāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam: Ayaʿjizu aḥadukum an yaksiba kulla yawmin alfa ḥasanatin? Fa saʾalahu sāʾilun min julasāʾihi kayfa yaksibu aḥadunā alfa ḥasanatin? Qāla: Yusabbihu miʾata tasbīḥatin, fa-yuktabu lahu alfu ḥasanatin aw yuḥaṭṭu ʿanhu alfu khaṭīʾatin.. And he (peace be upon him) said: \Is any one of you unable to earn a thousand good deeds every day?\"" A questioner among his companions asked"","" \""How can any of us earn a thousand good deeds?\"" He replied: \""He should glorify Allah one hundred times (by saying 'Subḥān Allāh')"","" and a thousand good deeds will be recorded for him"","" or a thousand sins will be erased from him.\"""
"259","Man qāla (subḥāna Allāhi al-ʿaẓīm wa bi-ḥamdihi) ghurisat lahu nakhlatun fī al-jannah.. Whoever says \Glory be to Allah the Almighty and praise be to Him"",""\"" a palm tree will be planted for him in Paradise."""
